  <tei:text>
    <tei:body>
      <tei:div corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:maran_divishmaya/captive">
        <tei:pb n="24" ed="1912" facs="https://archive.org/download/selichothdavidasher1912/page/n50_medium.jpg"/>
        <tei:p>Lord in heaven! unto thee we address our supplication, like a captive, who supplicates his master. All captives are ransomed with money, but thy people, the house of Israel, only by prayer and by supplication. O, grant our petition and our desire, and let us not return from thee empty-handed. </tei:p>
      </tei:div>
